Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: contrib/ras/ras2tif.c
Line: 95
Function: main
Bug type: buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-787
Explanation: datetime is a pointer to a string literal, but sprintf writes into it. Writing to read-only storage is undefined behavior and typically crashes. Use a writable buffer (e.g., char datetime[20]) and snprintf to avoid this.

